# wait-zero-next-pump: `wait 0 s` has its deadline at the reading of the Pump
# it ran in, which is already due. It still doesn't resume in that Pump,
# since timers fire only at a Pump's step 3, before its turns. The Pump
# reports it in `next`, and the next Pump fires it, even at the same reading,
# which isn't a Clock going backwards.
#
# Fuel (napper.talk): dispatch 4, const 1, wait 10; then const 1, return 2.
# Allocation and state figures are estimates.
# Unblessed: the output lines are written by hand, not by bless.

> load napper

> deliver d1 to=napper message=blink
> pump clock=2026-09-28T09:00:00Z
seg napper/r1 start delivery=d1 handler=blink clause=1 fuel=15 alloc=0 state=176 end=wait until=2026-09-28T09:00:00Z
pumped state=idle fuel=15 next=2026-09-28T09:00:00Z

# The same reading again: the wait is due, and fires.
> pump clock=2026-09-28T09:00:00Z
seg napper/r1 resume fuel=3 alloc=0 state=0 end=return
run napper/r1 outcome=completed delivery=d1 handler=blink value="blinked" fuel=18 alloc=0
pumped state=idle fuel=3

> vars
vars napper
